flowchart TB
    accTitle: Product X across successive decision cycles
    accDescr: A book-created two-cycle illustration begins with an HTTP 500 report. Planning produces and considers candidates, selection carries forward an inspection, and execution may make a hypothetical deployment timestamp available. The next cycle uses the available information to plan again. The timestamp is not a causal finding.

    subgraph CYCLE1[Decision cycle 1 - book-created example]
      direction TB
      WM1[Working information<br/>HTTP 500 report and investigation goal]
      PLAN1[Planning<br/>reasoning and optional retrieval]
      CANDS[Candidate set<br/>inspect deployment metadata<br/>query connectivity<br/>ask on-call engineer]
      SEL1[Evaluation and selection]
      EX1[Execute selected grounding action<br/>inspect deployment metadata]
      OBS1[Possible hypothetical observation<br/>deployment timestamp]
      WM1 --> PLAN1 --> CANDS --> SEL1 --> EX1
      EX1 -. response may be available .-> OBS1
    end
    subgraph CYCLE2[Decision cycle 2 - subsequent planning]
      direction TB
      WM2[Working information now includes<br/>any available observation]
      PLAN2[Plan again using current information]
      NEXT[Possible next decision<br/>query connectivity or choose a learning action]
      WM2 --> PLAN2 --> NEXT
    end
    OBS1 --> WM2

    classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef candidate fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef result fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px;
    class WM1,PLAN1,SEL1,EX1,PLAN2 process;
    class CANDS,NEXT candidate;
    class OBS1,WM2 result;
